From 38874ddc964b5741f9cd148fecd0d8548f62a794 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pom11 <parsecoriginalmastercraft@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:05:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): resolve a card whose active_pr PR is already
 merged

The dispatcher's active_pr respawn guard never asked GitHub anything, so a
card whose PR was already MERGED sat ready forever, burning a tick and
appending a respawn_guarded event every ~62 s (286-tick class, PR #703).

Add kanban_pr_acceptance.pr_merge_state(): one assignee-profile GraphQL read
of pullRequest{state mergedAt mergeCommit{oid}}, any failure -> UNKNOWN. The
dispatcher resolves a guarded card only on MERGED: complete it (or block
needs_input if completion is refused), append active_pr_resolved as a
terminal hold, and cache the probe per PR URL for 15 minutes. Dry runs never
probe or mutate, and the per-tick respawn_guarded row is deduped while the
in-memory bucket keeps reporting. OPEN/CLOSED/UNKNOWN keep holding exactly
as before; describe_suppression now also names the three skipped buckets so
a stuck warning is never reasonless.
